LibreDDRNet - third-party attribution
=====================================

Code
----

The DDRNet architecture in this family (``nn.py``) is ported from the official
implementation:

    Source:    https://github.com/ydhongHIT/DDRNet
    Commit:    de0db317c5af4b0946231f475cf74ca4f51b8ac2
    Files:     segmentation/DDRNet_23_slim.py, segmentation/DDRNet_23.py,
               segmentation/DDRNet_39.py
    License:   MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2020 xingkong

Module names follow upstream so the official checkpoints load after a key
rename (the ``model.`` training-wrapper prefix is stripped and the
``loss.criterion.weight`` buffer dropped); learned parameters are unchanged.
The residual blocks, DAPPM and segmentation head are shared with the in-tree
PIDNet port (``libreyolo/models/pidnet/nn.py``, MIT, XuJiacong/PIDNet), which
inherited them from DDRNet with identical definitions.

The OHEM cross-entropy and 0.4 auxiliary-loss recipe in ``loss.py`` follows the
paper ("Deep Dual-resolution Networks for Real-time and Accurate Semantic
Segmentation of Road Scenes", Hong et al., arXiv:2101.06085, section III-D and
IV-B); no upstream training code was copied.

Parity: weights/parity_ddrnet.py loads the official Cityscapes checkpoints into
the upstream ``DualResNet`` and into this port and asserts max_abs_diff == 0
for the main logits in eval mode and the main and auxiliary logits in train
mode; DDRNet-39 is checked on shared weights because upstream released no
Cityscapes DDRNet-39 checkpoint.

The LibreYOLO API surface, checkpoint integration, training integration, tests
and documentation are original work for this repository and are MIT-licensed
like the rest of LibreYOLO.

Weights
-------

Upstream links its checkpoints from its README (Google Drive) and states no
separate terms for them, so LibreYOLO hosts them under the repository's MIT
license on that implied basis. This is LibreYOLO's disclosed interpretation,
not a license confirmed by the publisher.

Converted Cityscapes checkpoints (19 classes), identified by the SHA-256 of
the upstream file:

  LibreDDRNets-sem.pt  DDRNet-23-slim, val mIoU 77.8 (upstream README)
      https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d_K3Af5fKHYwxSo8HkxpnhiekhwovmiP
      688dd42edbd623d21a6fe67c4b90ef8a5913d2824214a49bb60d94c61e6544b4
  LibreDDRNetm-sem.pt  DDRNet-23, val mIoU 79.5 (upstream README)
      https://drive.google.com/file/d/16viDZhbmuc3y7OSsUo2vhA7V6kYO0KX6
      66b68a4e61b2ab41fba5e967acd708ee3d9dd4771fb1e1a245a9a6b5bbd1db4e

These were trained on Cityscapes. The Cityscapes license
(https://www.cityscapes-dataset.com/license/) permits distributing abstract
derivative models from which the dataset cannot be recovered, and restricts
the dataset and its derivatives to NON-COMMERCIAL use. Check those terms before
using the pretrained Cityscapes checkpoints commercially. The dataset itself is
not redistributed by LibreYOLO. Weights trained from the ImageNet backbones or
from scratch on your own data carry no Cityscapes term; a fine-tune started
from a Cityscapes checkpoint inherits it.

Upstream released no Cityscapes DDRNet-39 checkpoint; size ``l`` is code-ready
and trains from its ImageNet backbone.

ImageNet-1K classifiers used to initialize training, mirrored byte-for-byte
under their upstream filenames:

  DDRNet23s_imagenet.pth (LibreYOLO/LibreDDRNets-imagenet)
      https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mg5tMX7TJ9ZVcAiGSB4PEihPtrJyalB4
      f6d03fa29b80e2e648f89a7639eb0c6d6c088e8f70f2cba1b2872b314a5c54b6
  DDRNet23_imagenet.pth (LibreYOLO/LibreDDRNetm-imagenet)
      https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VoUsERBeuCaiuQJufu8PqpKKtGvCTdug
      571959df93dce2db4b57d788362eb049a941e21b1b076a57112f8256216d1c08
  DDRNet39_imagenet.pth (LibreYOLO/LibreDDRNetl-imagenet)
      https://drive.google.com/file/d/122CMx6DZBaRRf-dOHYwuDY9vG0_UQ10i
